    </widget>
    <widget class="QLabel" name="label_12">
     <property name="geometry">
      <rect>
       <x>30</x>
       <y>290</y>
       <width>651</width>
       <height>121</height>
      </rect>
     </property>
     <property name="styleSheet">
      <string notr="true">font: 10pt &quot;Segoe UI&quot;;
color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
     </property>
     <property name="text">
      <string>Create a Dedicated Study Schedule 
 
Set specific times and durations for studying each day to build a habit. 
Example: Study math from 3–4 PM and take a 10-minute break before moving to another subject. 
Minimize Distractions</string>
     </property>
    </widget>
    <widget class="QLabel" name="label_11">
     <property name="geometry">
      <rect>
       <x>30</x>
       <y>70</y>
       <width>641</width>
       <height>221</height>
      </rect>
     </property>
     <property name="styleSheet">
      <string notr="true">font: 10pt &quot;Segoe UI&quot;;
color: rgb(0, 0, 0);</string>
     </property>
     <property name="text">
      <string> 
 Practice Active Recall 
Test yourself on key concepts instead of passively re-reading notes. 
Example: After studying a topic, close your book and try to explain it in your own words. 
Use Spaced Repetition 
 
Review material at gradually increasing intervals to improve long-term memory retention. 
Example: Use flashcards or apps like Anki to space out your study sessions effectively. 
Learn by Teaching 
 
Explain topics to others as if you’re teaching; it reinforces your understanding. 
Example: Form a study group and take turns teaching each other different topic</string>
     </property>
    </widget>
